capitalism. That's why I bought this

00:37:39.040 --> 00:37:43.520
property. I paid $160,000

00:37:41.720 --> 00:37:46.000
for this lot. At the time, it was worth

00:37:43.520 --> 00:37:48.280
about $300,000, and the reasons were

00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:49.440
twofold. Number one, this traffic. Yes,

00:37:48.280 --> 00:37:51.240
it's been a while since I bought this

00:37:49.440 --> 00:37:53.560
property, but this traffic was bad even

00:37:51.240 --> 00:37:55.920
back then. I live within 30 minutes of

00:37:53.560 --> 00:37:58.000
four of the fastest-growing cities in

00:37:55.920 --> 00:37:59.640
the country. The second reason I got a

00:37:58.000 --> 00:38:02.120
good deal for my property is because of

00:37:59.640 --> 00:38:03.960
the shape. It's very, very narrow. It's

00:38:02.120 --> 00:38:05.720
a weird shape. People didn't like it. It

00:38:03.960 --> 00:38:07.800
was unloved. It was unwanted. That's the

00:38:05.720 --> 00:38:10.200
whole purpose for this video. Today,

00:38:07.800 --> 00:38:12.280
this same lot, despite its location on a

00:38:10.200 --> 00:38:15.560
busy road, despite its awkward shape

00:38:12.280 --> 00:38:17.880
that it still has, is worth $750,000.

00:38:15.560 --> 00:38:19.680
It's far outpaced appreciation of the

00:38:17.880 --> 00:38:21.360
other homes and lots around here because

00:38:19.680 --> 00:38:24.360
I was willing to take that bet. How can

00:38:21.360 --> 00:38:26.400
you monetize 22,000 cars driving by a

00:38:24.360 --> 00:38:28.040
day? Where do I even begin? For my tree

00:38:26.400 --> 00:38:29.680
trimming business, I wrap my truck. I

00:38:28.040 --> 00:38:31.680
park it out here. Every time we have a

00:38:29.680 --> 00:38:34.160
car that we need to sell, I park it out

00:38:31.680 --> 00:38:36.000
here. If a car's worth $20,000 according

00:38:34.160 --> 00:38:39.040
to Kelly Blue Book value, I can sell it

00:38:36.000 --> 00:38:40.640
for $22,000 because more eyeballs equals

00:38:39.040 --> 00:38:42.360
more money. Think of it this way. If I

00:38:40.640 --> 00:38:44.440
was selling a widget and I tweeted about

00:38:42.360 --> 00:38:47.520
it to my 1,000 followers, that widget is

00:38:44.440 --> 00:38:49.440
worth $100. I can sell it for $100. If

00:38:47.520 --> 00:38:51.360
Elon Musk, the most followed person on

00:38:49.440 --> 00:38:53.360
Twitter, tweets about that same object

00:38:51.360 --> 00:38:56.520
for sale, what could he sell it for?

00:38:53.360 --> 00:38:58.160
$1,000? $300? No matter what it is, he

00:38:56.520 --> 00:39:00.320
could sell it for much more. Not because

00:38:58.160 --> 00:39:02.000
he's Elon Musk, but because of that many

00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:04.120
more eyeballs, millions of eyeballs

00:39:02.000 --> 00:39:06.360
seeing it. That's more demand. Fixed

00:39:04.120 --> 00:39:08.680
supply plus increasing demand equals

00:39:06.360 --> 00:39:10.120
increasing price. That's economics 101.

00:39:08.680 --> 00:39:12.160
So, I used to have a business called

00:39:10.120 --> 00:39:13.480
Presto Cars. It was a concierge car

00:39:12.160 --> 00:39:15.480
buying service. We would go to the

00:39:13.480 --> 00:39:17.680
Manheim and Adesa auctions and we would

00:39:15.480 --> 00:39:19.600
buy cars at wholesale, at the exact same

00:39:17.680 --> 00:39:21.680
price, the wholesale price that used

00:39:19.600 --> 00:39:24.120
auto dealerships get their cars for.

00:39:21.680 --> 00:39:27.120
Then, I would bring that car home. I'd

00:39:24.120 --> 00:39:28.560
pay $13,000 for it. I would park it

00:39:27.120 --> 00:39:30.920
right there with a for sale sign and I

00:39:28.560 --> 00:39:33.560
would sell it for $17,000. You do that

00:39:30.920 --> 00:39:35.240
once a week, that's $16,000 a month of

00:39:33.560 --> 00:39:37.360
net profit. Are there headaches? Of

00:39:35.240 --> 00:39:39.440
course. I ran out of gas. They would

00:39:37.360 --> 00:39:41.920
break down. It was a pain, but it was

00:39:39.440 --> 00:39:44.600
profitable and it was all made possible

00:39:41.920 --> 00:39:47.280
because of this lot that gets 22,000

00:39:44.600 --> 00:39:49.440
cars, 22,000 eyeballs driving by it

00:39:47.280 --> 00:39:51.800
every single day. So, that's why this is

00:39:49.440 --> 00:39:55.600
my number one favorite idea because of

00:39:51.800 --> 00:39:57.640
the optionality. If you buy a lot,

00:39:55.600 --> 00:39:59.600
especially if it's zoned residential,

00:39:57.640 --> 00:40:01.800
because residential buyers do not value

00:39:59.600 --> 00:40:03.200
this. In fact, they don't like traffic.

00:40:01.800 --> 00:40:04.760
But if you're willing to look at it from

00:40:03.200 --> 00:40:06.800
a capitalistic perspective, a

00:40:04.760 --> 00:40:09.480
monetization perspective, then you can

00:40:06.800 --> 00:40:11.680
sell anything you want. Billboard, cars,

00:40:09.480 --> 00:40:13.640
signage, wrapped vehicles, farm stand,

00:40:11.680 --> 00:40:15.560
lemonade, waters, it doesn't matter.

00:40:13.640 --> 00:40:17.760
Best and highest use. So, every time I

00:40:15.560 --> 00:40:19.880
see these cars out front, I smile to

00:40:17.760 --> 00:40:21.360
myself and think, "Capitalism." If you

00:40:19.880 --> 00:40:24.040
live in the United States, you need to

00:40:21.360 --> 00:40:27.120
look into what's called the USDA Rural

00:40:24.040 --> 00:40:29.560
Development Loan. This loan has no PMI,

00:40:27.120 --> 00:40:32.520
no mortgage insurance, as in less fees,

00:40:29.560 --> 00:40:34.240
and if your land or property is in a

00:40:32.520 --> 00:40:35.560
specific area, there's a map online

00:40:34.240 --> 00:40:37.120
where you can look at all this. If it's

00:40:35.560 --> 00:40:38.800
in an area and your credit is not

00:40:37.120 --> 00:40:39.920
terrible, it doesn't have to be amazing,

00:40:38.800 --> 00:40:41.760
but if it's not terrible, you can

00:40:39.920 --> 00:40:44.640
qualify for 0% down for a

00:40:41.760 --> 00:40:46.160
government-backed loan through most

00:40:44.640 --> 00:40:47.880
legitimate banks. There are some

00:40:46.160 --> 00:40:50.360
restrictions. One of the restrictions is

00:40:47.880 --> 00:40:52.760
you can only use it on raw land if you

00:40:50.360 --> 00:40:54.280
plan to build a building or a piece of

00:40:52.760 --> 00:40:56.400
real estate on it. I believe it does

00:40:54.280 --> 00:40:58.240
qualify for stick-built homes, modular

00:40:56.400 --> 00:40:59.920
homes, and manufactured homes. There are

00:40:58.240 --> 00:41:01.680
income limits, but the interest rates

00:40:59.920 --> 00:41:03.680
are even lower than FHA loans. And if

00:41:01.680 --> 00:41:05.640
you want only raw land and to never put

00:41:03.680 --> 00:41:06.920
anything on it, this will unfortunately

00:41:05.640 --> 00:41:09.320
not work for you. You should also look

00:41:06.920 --> 00:41:12.080
into master lease agreements. It doesn't

00:41:09.320 --> 00:41:14.480
always apply to only raw land, but I've

00:41:12.080 --> 00:41:15.960
used this on some RV park deals where

00:41:14.480 --> 00:41:17.720
let's say you can't afford to buy the

00:41:15.960 --> 00:41:19.400
land cash or you can't find a loan or

00:41:17.720 --> 00:41:21.240
you can't afford a down payment. You

00:41:19.400 --> 00:41:23.800
basically make lease payments to the

00:41:21.240 --> 00:41:26.000
owner, but all of the cash flow over and

00:41:23.800 --> 00:41:27.760
above those lease payments go to you.

00:41:26.000 --> 00:41:29.760
This is very similar to a lease purchase

00:41:27.760 --> 00:41:32.000
agreement in that it enables you to

00:41:29.760 --> 00:41:35.080
lessen your risk before going all in on

00:41:32.000 --> 00:41:36.880
an asset. And then later on, 1 3 5 years

00:41:35.080 --> 00:41:38.920
down the line, you have the option to

00:41:36.880 --> 00:41:41.400
purchase the property and or business on

00:41:38.920 --> 00:41:43.120
the property at a predetermined price if

00:41:41.400 --> 00:41:44.560
it has been going well thus far. Bonus

00:41:43.120 --> 00:41:47.120
idea for you. I have a friend in North

00:41:44.560 --> 00:41:49.120
